This folder contains Fortran Code to extract POD modes.

The code is based on an existing piece of code "Empirical Orthogonal Function (EOF) software/Principal Component Analysis (PCA) software" by David W. Pierce, Climate Research Division, Scripps Institution of Oceanography. See http://meteora.ucsd.edu/~pierce/eof/eofs.html

A copy of which is available inside original_version_pierce

With respect to this code we introduced the following modifications:
- Updated from F77 to Modern Fortran
- Inputs are modified to read 2-D DNS from Basilisk. Snapshots are given in the binary matrix format read directly by gnuplot (see http://gnuplot.sourceforge.net/docs_4.2/node330.html)

 Single precision floats are stored in a binary file as follows:


     <N+1>  <y0>   <y1>   <y2>  ...  <yN>
      <x0> <z0,0> <z0,1> <z0,2> ... <z0,N>
      <x1> <z1,0> <z1,1> <z1,2> ... <z1,N>
       :      :      :      :   ...    :

 which are converted into triplets:

     <x0> <y0> <z0,0>
     <x0> <y1> <z0,1>
     <x0> <y2> <z0,2>
      :    :     :
     <x0> <yN> <z0,N>



     <x1> <y0> <z1,0>
     <x1> <y1> <z1,1>
      :    :     :

- Different formulations of POD are considered. Based on the velocity, temperature or joint velocity-temperature as described in the Thesis.  

- A makefile is included with examples 
>> make clean
>> make try
>> make proj

